      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T16:04:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW, the direct inclusion into GLSL is only for the hardware tessellation backdoor. Graphite won\u0027t use HW tessellation, and it\u0027s a little on life support right now in ganesh, with plans to remove it when it becomes worth more to take the time to clean it up compared to keeping it running.\n\nIf this would let us clean up the sksl side of things as well, it may be time to commit to removing that tessellator.",
      "revId": "fe0976d38b1ad52c1e6703219cdf0f6f1419a857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21bb8ba4_2f5864a6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T16:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t HW tessellation critical for the MotionMark benchmarks?\n\nI think it\u0027d be safer to move the SkSL chunks into /ganesh/ and put off dismantling it until we have a compelling replacement story. (Tangentially, Ethan plans to investigate compute shaders this quarter.)",
      "parentUuid": "8037f7aa_cc7b866d",
      "revId": "fe0976d38b1ad52c1e6703219cdf0f6f1419a857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5fe8421a_62d6416e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T17:00:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, Chris\u0027 2nd (3rd? 4th?) generation didn\u0027t rely on HW tessellation anymore - it uses simpler API techniques, with some very clever pre-built geometry and vertex shading. (It does require some pre-processing steps to bin/sort the paths, which is work that we hope to move to compute shaders).",
      "parentUuid": "21bb8ba4_2f5864a6",
      "revId": "fe0976d38b1ad52c1e6703219cdf0f6f1419a857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2220715c_b35ff65b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T17:00:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using the tessellation shaders is not critical for MotionMark. On some platforms it is worse performance, some neutral, and some slight better. The key thing is to do all the vertex calculations on the GPU instead of the CPU. But this can be done using the vertex shaders and just uploading N vertices (some of which may just get thrown away as degenerate triangles)",
      "parentUuid": "21bb8ba4_2f5864a6",
      "revId": "fe0976d38b1ad52c1e6703219cdf0f6f1419a857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a5feaa8_6ff8a833",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
